From bef4da188b567de5b8ec4f7fbfc8d9dcfb8b01f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:39:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] jm-v7 016: Bifrost pipeline statistics and transform
 feedback queries

pipelineStatisticsQuery and transformFeedbackQueries on v6/v7, counted on
the GPU in the v9 JM report layout (two u64 per statistic, the second
half written by kernels and shaders, results are the sum):

- IA vertices/primitives, VS invocations, TCS patches, and clipping
  without a geometry shader: panlib_v7_update_pstats_draw(), one thread
  per draw from its Vk[Indexed]DrawIndirectCommand (written at record
  time for vkCmdDraw). Primitive restart is counted by a serial index
  scan: the v9 subgroup scan needs 16-wide subgroups. The tess eval draw
  of a tessellated draw counts the TES invocations (one per tessellator
  index, which is how the TES runs).
- Geometry shader invocations/primitives, and clipping after a geometry
  shader: the emulation adds them itself at the end of every live
  invocation (panvk_gs_push::pstats, a table of four counter addresses).
  The xfb passthrough does not count as a geometry shader.
- Fragment shader invocations: the hardware occlusion counter, while no
  occlusion query owns it, as on v9 JM. Bifrost writes it per core, so it
  points at a per-query scratch (one u64 per core, zeroed by GPU write
  jobs) that panlib_v7_pstats_sum_cores() adds into the report at
  vkCmdEndQuery.
- Compute shader invocations: panlib_v7_update_pstats_dispatch().
- Transform feedback stream queries: panlib_xfb_scan adds the primitives
  written and needed of its stream to the active query
  (libpan_xfb_draw::query). A stream that captures to no buffer is still
  scanned when a query is active.

The query pool, vkGetQueryPoolResults and the GPU copy
(panlib_copy_pstats_query_result) take the v9 paths on v6/v7.

ponytail (same as v9 JM): FS invocations miss fragments killed by late
ZS, count samples with MSAA, and are not counted while an occlusion
query is active. Layered (non-multiview) draws count layer 0 only.
vk_meta draws are not counted.

Not device-tested.
